  "blocks": {
    "\"Have the planner write a handoff artifact — file paths, decisions, constraints. The implementer's session opens with a pointer to the artifact and works from it as its brief.\"": "“让规划者编写一份交接产物，记录文件路径、决策和约束。实现者的会话从指向该产物的上下文指针开始，并把它作为任务简报。”",
    "\"How do I split this between the planning agent and the implementing one?\"": "“如何把这项工作分给规划<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/agent\">智能体</a>和实现智能体？”",
    "A document used as the carry mechanism for a handoff — written to the environment by one session to be read by another. Specs, tickets, and plan docs are all handoff artifacts.": "交接产物是用于承载<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/handoff\">交接</a>信息的文档：由一次<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/session\">会话</a>写入<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/environment\">环境</a>，再由另一次会话读取。<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/spec\">规格说明</a>、<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/ticket\">任务</a>和计划文档都属于交接产物。",
    "A good artifact is written to be read into a session that has zero context. Concrete file paths rather than \"the file we discussed\". What was decided and why, so the next session doesn't relitigate it. What's done and what's left. It helps to tell the writing session where the artifact is headed: \"write a handoff doc for a fresh session that knows nothing about this work\".": "优秀的交接产物应当假设读者是一个零上下文会话。使用明确文件路径，而不是“我们讨论过的那个文件”；记录作出了什么决定以及原因，避免下一次会话重新争论；说明已经完成什么、还剩什么。告诉写作会话这份文档将被谁使用也很有帮助，例如：“为一个对当前工作一无所知的新会话编写交接文档。”",
    "The alternative carry mechanism is compaction, which summarises in-memory. The artifact has two advantages: it lives on disk where you can read and correct it before anything depends on it, and it can be reused — the same spec can brief five parallel sessions.": "另一种承载机制是<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/compaction\">压缩</a>，它在内存中生成摘要。交接产物有两个优势：它存放在磁盘上，可以在后续工作依赖它之前由你阅读并修正；它还可以复用——同一份规格说明可以同时为五个并行会话提供背景。",
    "The artifact is a secondary source — an account of the session's work, not the work itself. That's what makes it small enough to brief a fresh session, and also why it can mislead one: it records what the writing session believed, and anything it left out or got wrong is invisible to the reader. Where a claim matters, the next session should verify it against the primary source — the code, the tests — rather than inherit it.": "交接产物属于<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/secondary-source\">二手来源</a>——它记述一次会话完成的工作，但并不是工作本身。这使它足够精简，可以快速向新会话说明情况；同时也意味着它可能误导读者：文档记录的是写作会话当时相信的内容，任何遗漏或错误对后续读者都不可见。只要某项陈述很重要，下一次会话就应对照<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/primary-source\">一手来源</a>——代码和测试——进行验证，而不是直接继承。",
    "The reason to write one: the model is stateless, so nothing in a session survives clearing it. Decisions, constraints, half-finished plans — all gone with the context that held them. The environment persists. Writing the important state into a file moves it somewhere the next session can read it back from.": "之所以需要写交接产物，是因为<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/model\">模型</a>是<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/stateless\">无状态</a>的；会话一旦<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/clearing\">清空</a>，其中没有任何内容能够自动保留。决策、约束、尚未完成的计划，都会随承载它们的<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/context\">上下文</a>一起消失。环境却会持续存在。把重要状态写入文件，就是把它移动到下一次会话能够重新读取的位置。",
    "Usage:": "<em>用法：</em>"
  },
